window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["10"]={"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/botswana":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"5224f92d62ba4aadbaa1723b3c5e1f477654321c555cf665f961121ecab5ed09","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/botswana","bytes":56188,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Botswana travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-01-10T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-11-06T14:39:38+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/botswana/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Botswana’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Botswana set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Botswana High Commission in the UK","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/foreign-embassies-in-the-uk"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 0207 499 0031"]},{"k":"p","s":["Email: bohico@govbw.com"]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Botswana, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive and at least 3 blank pages."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you get your passport stamped."]},{"k":"p","s":["This will record your date and port of entry. Unstamped passports will raise suspicions of illegal entry."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dual nationals must enter Botswana on the same passport they used to exit the previous country."]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can visit Botswana for up to 90 days without a visa."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you want to work, study or volunteer in Botswana, see the ",["requirements for business, study and employment visas","https://www.gov.bw/immigration-civil-registration?txterm=114"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Overstaying a visa or a permitted visit can cause a delay to your departure. If you want to extend your stay, contact Botswana’s ",["Department of Immigration","https://www.gov.bw/contact-us"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travelling with children"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must carry the original or a certified copy of the full birth certificate for any child aged 17 or under entering or leaving Botswana."]},{"k":"p","s":["If a child is travelling with only one parent, with a guardian or another adult, or alone, carry the required parental consent or documents showing authority to travel. If parental consent is required, also carry a certified copy of the consenting parent’s passport or identity document."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use GOV.UK guidance to ",["find a notary in the UK","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/find-a-notary-abroad"],". In Botswana, police stations can help with affidavits of consent. You can also use ",["Find a professional service abroad","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers"]," to find an English-speaking lawyer."]},{"k":"p","s":["For more information, contact the ",["Botswana High Commission in the UK","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/foreign-embassies-in-the-uk"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Botswana, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For more details about health entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Botswana guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/33/botswana#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ebola"]},{"k":"p","s":["As a public health measure, Botswana has introduced entry restrictions including health screening for travellers arriving from affected regions. ",["Check entry requirements","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice"]," for the country you’re travelling to or transiting."]},{"k":"p","s":["The World Health Organisation (WHO) have ",["declared Ebola as a Public Health Emergency of International Concern","https://www.who.int/news/item/17-05-2026-epidemic-of-ebola-disease-in-the-democratic-republic-of-the-congo-and-uganda-determined-a-public-health-emergency-of-international-concern"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of Botswana. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Botswana"]},{"k":"p","s":["Declare foreign or local cash currency if the value is 10,000 Botswana pula or more. If you do not, you could be liable to prosecution."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Botswana"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Botswana, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks on tourists are rare, but violent crime is increasing particularly in the major towns of Gaborone, Francistown and Maun. Criminals have also carried out hold-ups and robberies of restaurants during peak hours."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Criminals may target cars waiting at traffic lights. To reduce the risk of attack:"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep doors locked and windows closed"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep handbags, phones and laptops out of sight"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid carrying luggage in your vehicle whenever possible"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not stop for people at the roadside hitchhiking"]},{"k":"p","s":["House burglaries, often by armed gangs, are common. They do not often target tourists, but there have been isolated room break-ins and theft from lodges in the Chobe area, particularly river-fronting lodges. To reduce the risk of burglary or home invasion:"]},{"k":"li","s":["lock your room at all times"]},{"k":"li","s":["speak to your travel operator if your accommodation does not seem secure"]},{"k":"li","s":["secure valuables in a hotel safe or other safe place"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sexual assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["Botswana has a high number of sexual assaults. While foreign visitors are unlikely to be targeted, women should take care when walking and avoid walking alone at night."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always carry some identification. A copy of the photo page in your passport is usually enough as long as you can produce the original if required."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you send your passport for renewal, make sure you have a certified copy that you can present in its place."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Drug taking and trafficking are illegal. If you’re convicted of a drug-related offence, you can get a fine of up to 500,000 pulas (about £30,000) or a prison sentence of up to 25 years, or both. Prison conditions are generally poor."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to take photographs or use video equipment near military and government installations. Always ask permission before photographing people in Botswana."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although same-sex sexual activity is no longer prohibited by law, public attitudes are less tolerant than in the UK and displaying affection in public may attract negative attention."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildlife, animal products and souvenirs"]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s illegal to buy, sell, kill or capture any protected wild animal or trade its parts. If you’re caught hunting, buying or trafficking these goods you will be prosecuted. If you’re convicted, sentences can be severe."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you travel to remote areas, make transport and accommodation arrangements in advance and seek local security advice. Take emergency supplies, including water and fuel, and be prepared for off-road driving conditions. In very remote areas, travel in convoy or with a satellite phone in case of breakdown."]},{"k":"p","s":["On open highways, inside or outside wildlife reserves, there could be dangerous animals roaming that may behave unpredictably. Always follow park regulations and advice from park wardens."]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not bathe in rivers and lakes. You could be attacked by wild animals and you risk catching water-borne diseases."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Botswana. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["1949 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can drive with a UK driving licence for up to 90 days. If you intend to stay longer than 90 days, apply for a Botswana driving licence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hire car companies often have stricter requirements for their customers, such as a year of driving experience, a higher minimum age and holding an IDP."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Botswana has good tarmac roads covering most of the country, but driving outside the major urban areas can be dangerous due to stray wildlife and livestock. This is a particular risk at night, so take extra care if you’re driving after dark."]},{"k":"p","s":["The standard of driving is lower than in the UK. Many drivers ignore rules of the road. Speeding and drink-driving, or driving on drugs, cause frequent and often fatal accidents."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["To reduce risk of crime when using taxis, look for licensed taxis with blue plate numbers. Cabs run by a recognised taxi company will usually have branding and can be pre-booked."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["Botswana’s rainy season, runs from November to March, bringing heavy rainfalls and risk of flash flooding. Road conditions throughout the country may be unsafe. Follow the advice of ",["Botswana’s Meteorological Services","https://www.facebook.com/BotswanaMet"]," and from the local authorities at ",["Ministry of Environment and Tourism","https://www.facebook.com/people/Ministry-of-Environment-and-Tourism-Botswana/61569658071888/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Floodings may also impact border crossings with closure at short notice. Follow the advice of ",["Botswana’s Unified Revenue Services","https://www.facebook.com/BotswanaUnifiedRevenueService"]," for latest updates on road accessibility and border opening and closure status."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 997 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Botswana","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/33/botswana#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Botswana","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/33/botswana"]," including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["malaria, which is reported in April 2025 to have spread to areas where it is not usually present"]},{"k":"li","s":["schistosomiasis"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are occasional outbreaks of anthrax among wild animals. Do not touch dead animals or carcases. If you suspect that you have come into contact with anthrax, seek urgent medical advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you intend to camp or walk in the bush, take precautions to avoid tick bites, as they can cause several dangerous diseases."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Botswana"]},{"k":"p","s":["The State of Public Health Emergency is now over. Despite this, medicine and medical supply shortages remain widespread across public health facilities nationwide. Private healthcare remains largely unaffected."]},{"k":"p","s":["Healthcare in Botswana is usually good in major towns, but medical facilities and communications are limited in rural areas. For serious medical treatment, medical evacuation to the UK or South Africa may be necessary."]},{"k":"p","s":["Private hospitals will not treat you unless you can pay, and the cost may be high. Public hospitals will only take you as an emergency patient if you have full insurance. For outpatient treatment, you will need to pay up front."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Botswana","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/botswana-list-of-medical-facilities/botswana-list-of-medical-facilities"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Botswana"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 997"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 998"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 999"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding ",["lawyers in Botswana","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Botswana"]]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Botswana","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/what-to-do-after-a-british-person-dies-in-botswana"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Botswana","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/botswana-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/botswana/british-high-commission-gaborone"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/botswana/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":13535,"change":"Updated information about the documents needed when travelling with children (see 'Travelling with children' on the 'Entry requirements' page)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/western-sahara":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:38Z","sha":"d696847051e8c34b871e651ed6b2942034c9958238edcb69e65943ab4bbf1301","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/western-sahara","bytes":38139,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Western Sahara travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-02-05T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-06-29T14:34:01+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against all travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Areas in Western Sahara within 40km North and West of ‘the Berm’ boundary line, including the city of Es Semara"]},{"k":"li","s":["Areas in Western Sahara the territory south and east of ‘the Berm’ boundary line"]},{"k":"p","s":["Western Sahara is a disputed territory. The Berm is the militarised boundary between Moroccan-controlled Western Sahara and territory to the east controlled by the Polisario Front. Cross border rocket fire has occurred which cannot be ruled out in the future."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["why FCDO advises against travel","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/western-sahara/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/western-sahara/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Western Sahara’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Western Sahara set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Moroccan Consulate General in the UK","https://www.consulat.ma/en"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your passport must be valid for the proposed duration of your stay."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can travel without a visa for visits to the Moroccan-administered parts of Western Sahara and Morocco for up to 90 days."]},{"k":"p","s":["Travel is restricted. Organised groups are generally permitted, but independent travellers could be turned back at the border."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you get your passport stamped."]},{"k":"p","s":["When first arriving in Morocco/Western Sahara, make sure you get a passport stamp from the Moroccan border control authorities. You may have difficulty leaving the country without a stamp."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Western Sahara guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/245/western-sahara#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of Western Sahara. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty. Check ",["Moroccan customs rules","https://www.douane.gov.ma/web/guest/particuliers"]," (in French) for the Moroccan-administered parts of Western Sahara."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Western Sahara"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are likely to try to carry out attacks in Western Sahara."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places visited by foreign nationals. Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Western Sahara is on the UN list of Non-Self-Governing Territories and the subject of a UN-mediated dispute. The UN Peacekeeping mission for Western Sahara, MINURSO, has been operating in the country since 1991. A ceasefire between Morocco and the Polisario Front broke down in 2020. Irregular skirmishes continue to take place between the 2 sides, sometimes resulting in civilian casualties."]},{"k":"p","s":["Most of Western Sahara is under administration of Morocco, which closely monitors and controls access to the territory. You should avoid political gatherings and demonstrations."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow any media reporting and instructions from local security authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Western Sahara is predominantly Muslim. Always respect local traditions, customs, laws and religion. Make sure your actions do not offend, especially during the holy month of Ramadan or if you plan to visit religious areas."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ramadan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ramadan is a holy month for Muslims. The dates vary by year and country, so check when Ramadan is in Western Sahara before you go. During this time, do not:"]},{"k":"li","s":["eat, drink, smoke or chew gum in public in the daytime, including in your car"]},{"k":"li","s":["play loud music or dance"]},{"k":"li","s":["swear in public"]},{"k":"p","s":["Get more advice when you arrive from your tour guide, hotel or business contacts."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check opening hours of shops and restaurants"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that if hotels and restaurants are providing food or drink in fasting hours, they may separate you from Islamic guests, for example with screens"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow local dress codes – clothing that doesn’t meet local dress codes may cause more offence at this time"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that driving may be erratic, particularly when people are trying to get home at dusk"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Laws against religious conversion"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to attempt to convert any Muslim to another faith or to distribute evangelical literature, such as Arabic-language bibles. Attempting to convert a Muslim to another faith is punishable by fines or up to 3 years in prison."]},{"k":"p","s":["Criticism of Islam on public platforms, in print or online media, or in public speeches is punishable by heavy fines and up to 2 years in prison."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sexual relations outside of marriage"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sexual activity between unmarried people and adultery are illegal – this includes sharing a hotel room."]},{"k":"p","s":["The law against unmarried people sharing a hotel room does not generally apply to visiting foreign nationals, particularly in popular tourist areas."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is illegal. Be sensitive to local laws and customs and avoid showing affection in public. Complaints can lead to prosecution."]},{"k":"p","s":["See more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Women travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Women may receive unwanted attention from men, especially when travelling alone. Consider wearing loose-fitting clothing which cover the arms, legs and chest. See ",["advice for women travelling abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol laws"]},{"k":"p","s":["Licensed hotels, restaurants and bars serve alcohol in tourist areas. Drinking alcohol in the street or anywhere other than licensed premises is illegal and can lead to arrest."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Western Sahara, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You’ll need to have both the ",["1968 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," and your UK driving licence with you in the car. You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are staying in Western Sahara for longer than one year, you must apply for a ",["Moroccan driving licence","https://consulat.ma/en/driving-license"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re planning to hire a car, check with your car hire company for information on their requirements before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["Drive carefully, especially when:"]},{"k":"li","s":["driving at night, which be particularly dangerous due to poor lighting"]},{"k":"li","s":["weather conditions are poor on secondary routes and mountain roads"]},{"k":"li","s":["overtaking lorries and trucks that are overloaded and when there is no hard shoulder"]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Western Sahara. It only covers regions where the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/western-sahara"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/western-sahara/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Landmines, unexploded weapons and rocket fire"]},{"k":"p","s":["A militarised boundary known as ‘the Berm’ separates the Moroccan-administered part of Western Sahara from the rest of the territory. There are 30km militarised zones either side of the Berm containing landmines. There have been many fatalities in these zones. Cross border rocket fire has occurred which cannot be ruled out in the future."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Areas in Western Sahara within 40km North and West of ‘the Berm’ boundary line, including the city of Es Semara"]},{"k":"li","s":["Areas in Western Sahara the territory south and east of ‘the Berm’ boundary line"]},{"k":"p","s":["The eastern side of the Berm is sparsely populated with no diplomatic presence from any country. There are other types of unexploded weapons in this area."]},{"k":"p","s":["In remote areas:"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep to main roads and stay alert"]},{"k":"li","s":["if you drive off the main roads, keep to clearly identifiable tracks"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not touch any metal or plastic objects"]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 150 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Western Sahara","https://www.travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/245/western-sahara#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Western Sahara","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/245/western-sahara"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Western Sahara"]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical facilities are adequate in the main cities – Laayoune, Dhakla and Smara – all of which have hospitals, clinics and pharmacies. For more sophisticated medical treatment, including scans, you will need to go to a major centre in Morocco or the Canary Islands."]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical facilities are almost non-existent in desert areas. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Western Sahara"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 150 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/western-sahara/british-embassy-rabat"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/western-sahara/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":12242,"change":"FCDO now advises against all travel to areas in Western Sahara within 40km North and West of 'the Berm' boundary line, including the city of Es Semara ('Warnings and insurance' page)."},"https://theconversation.com/mengapa-pemimpin-otoriter-dan-antikritik-kerap-banyak-pemujanya-294906":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"1ff7883300749e2bee843795011ea4a8bc17ede79328aaf05927ffe7ba29a0dc","read":"https://theconversation.com/mengapa-pemimpin-otoriter-dan-antikritik-kerap-banyak-pemujanya-294906","bytes":178824,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Mengapa pemimpin otoriter dan antikritik kerap banyak pemujanya?","by":[{"n":"Nayunda Andhika Sari","r":"Lecturer in Management and Organisation Studies, Universitas Indonesia"},{"n":"Kanti Pertiwi","r":"Assistant Professor in Organisation Studies, Universitas Indonesia"}],"pub":"2026-11-13T02:16:50Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["• Pemimpin dominan kerap dianggap kompeten, tapi bisa membungkam kritik dan perbedaan pendapat."]},{"k":"p","s":["• Budaya organisasi dan masyarakat ikut melanggengkan kepemimpinan heroik dan antikritik."]},{"k":"p","s":["• Kepemimpinan perlu mengutamakan kolaborasi dan memberi ruang bagi semua orang untuk bersuara."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pemimpin yang membentak bawahan di depan umum kerap dipandang tegas oleh sebagian kalangan. Begitu pula pejabat yang mengambil keputusan sepihak masih sering dianggap berani. Sementara itu, pemimpin yang mengakui kesalahan atau meminta masukan justru berisiko dicap lemah."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pandangan ini menunjukkan betapa kuatnya anggapan bahwa ",["pemimpin ideal","https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/1048984394900051"]," harus dominan, berkarisma, dan selalu memiliki jawaban atas setiap persoalan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Masalahnya, ketegasan sering disamakan dengan kemampuan memimpin, sementara kepatuhan dianggap sebagai bukti keberhasilan kepemimpinan. Akibatnya, perilaku otoriter bisa memperoleh dukungan, sekalipun itu bisa merugikan organisasi dan masyarakat."]},{"k":"p","s":["Mengapa pola ini terus bertahan? Duduk permasalahan ini bukan semata berasal dari karakter pemimpin, tetapi juga pengaruh budaya yang membentuk, memuja, dan mempertahankan tradisi ini."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dominasi dianggap kompetensi"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dalam kajian kepemimpinan, kecenderungan menempatkan pemimpin sebagai sosok luar biasa yang menentukan keberhasilan organisasi dikenal sebagai ",["heroic leadership (kepemimpinan heroik)","https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/abs/10.1080/00220620.2010.492959"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Perspektif ini menganggap keberhasilan terutama berasal dari keberanian, kecerdasan, dan keputusan seorang pemimpin. Kontribusi pekerja, kondisi organisasi, serta faktor sosial dan politik kerap terabaikan."]},{"k":"p","s":[["https://www.facebook.com/reel/1557882292118422","https://www.facebook.com/reel/1557882292118422"]]},{"k":"p","s":[["Penelitian tentang kategorisasi kepemimpinan","https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/0030507384900436?"]," menunjukkan bahwa manusia memiliki gambaran tertentu tentang karakter pemimpin ideal. Gambaran tersebut memengaruhi siapa yang dianggap layak memimpin."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ketika dominasi diagungkan, orang yang berbicara paling keras atau tampil paling percaya diri lebih mudah dianggap kompeten. Padahal belum tentu."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dalam masyarakat dengan hierarki kekuasaan yang kuat, kecenderungan ini berpotensi semakin mengakar."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kita bisa melihatnya dalam keseharian. Di kantor, atasan yang mendominasi rapat dianggap berwibawa. Sementara bawahan yang mempertanyakan keputusan dicap tidak loyal."]},{"k":"p","s":["Di ruang publik, video pejabat memarahi staf bisa memperoleh pujian karena dianggap menunjukkan ketegasan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Padahal, kemampuan mempermalukan bawahan bukan ukuran kompetensi, apalagi keberhasilan kebijakan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Masalah semakin serius ketika organisasi ikut mempertahankan pola tersebut. Bawahan memilih diam demi menjaga karier atau menjilat pemimpin karena yakin posisinya tak tergoyahkan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Fenomena ini berkaitan dengan employee silence, yakni kecenderungan pekerja menahan informasi, kekhawatiran, atau kritik terhadap organisasi. ",["Riset tentang psikologi organisasi","https://www.annualreviews.org/content/journals/10.1146/annurev-orgpsych-031413-091328"]," menjelaskan bahwa ketakutan terhadap konsekuensi negatif menjadi salah satu alasan pekerja enggan bersuara."]},{"k":"p","s":["Nyatanya pemimpin antikritik tidak selalu bertahan karena dianggap berhasil. Mereka juga bisa terus memperoleh legitimasi karena lingkungan membuat kritik terasa berisiko."]},{"k":"h","s":["Kepemimpinan bukan pertunjukan satu orang"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dominasi pemimpin semakin mudah dipasarkan melalui media sosial."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Konten pejabat","https://theconversation.com/viral-dulu-substansi-belakangan-3-risiko-punya-pemimpin-politik-kreator-konten-259378"]," yang melakukan inspeksi mendadak, memarahi bawahan, atau menunjukkan aksi simbolis dapat membangun citra sebagai penyelamat. Namun, popularitas tindakan tersebut tidak otomatis membuktikan efektivitas kebijakan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ketika perhatian hanya tertuju pada figur, pangkal persoalan utama sering luput dari perhatian: apakah persoalan terselesaikan? kebijakannya berdampak? dan siapa yang menanggung akibat keputusan tersebut?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Di sinilah pentingnya perspektif ",["post-heroic leadership","https://www.amazon.com/Shared-Leadership-Reframing-Hows-Whys/dp/0761926240/ref=mt_paperback?_encoding=UTF8&me="],". Berbeda dengan kepemimpinan heroik, pendekatan ini melihat kepemimpinan sebagai ",["proses kolektif","https://www.amazon.com/Shared-Leadership-Reframing-Hows-Whys/dp/0761926240/ref=mt_paperback?_encoding=UTF8&me="]," yang melibatkan hubungan, kerja sama, dan pembagian pengaruh, bukan kehebatan satu individu."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Kajian Fletcher","https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1048984304000827"]," menekankan pentingnya praktik kepemimpinan yang lebih relasional dan tidak bergantung pada figur tunggal. Artinya, pemimpin tetap memiliki tanggung jawab mengambil keputusan, tetapi tidak memonopoli pengetahuan dan kewenangan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dalam penanganan krisis, misalnya, pemimpin yang efektif bukan yang paling lantang menyalahkan bawahan atau ",["“asbun” (asal bunyi)","https://theconversation.com/pejabat-bukan-gen-alpha-asbun-mereka-saat-asap-karhutla-bukan-salah-ucap-tapi-krisis-empati-294869"],", tetapi yang mendengarkan ahli, menerima laporan lapangan, mengakui kesalahan, dan memperbaiki kebijakan berdasarkan bukti."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pendekatan ini juga penting bagi organisasi. ",["Penelitian Edmondson (1999)","https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.2307/2666999"]," menunjukkan bahwa psychological safety, yakni rasa aman untuk mengambil risiko interpersonal, berkaitan dengan perilaku belajar dalam tim."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dengan kata lain, ruang untuk bertanya, berbeda pendapat, dan mengakui kesalahan bukan ancaman bagi kepemimpinan, melainkan bagian penting dari organisasi yang mampu belajar."]},{"k":"h","s":["Berhenti memuja jabatan, mulai memperkuat kritik"]},{"k":"p","s":["Mengubah budaya kepemimpinan tidak cukup dengan meminta pejabat lebih rendah hati. Kita pun perlu ",["mengurangi pendewaan dan penghormatan kepada kekuasaan","https://books.google.com.bh/books?hl=en&lr=&id=ZXX3CgAAQBAJ&oi=fnd&pg=PT7&dq=The+Stupidity+Paradox&ots=t-SOtvdUaf&sig=cLddZvqCAk1opljJPNEm8xg4tQc&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q&f=false"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Di lingkungan kerja, misalnya, rapat seharusnya memberi ruang bagi pekerja untuk menyampaikan pandangan berbeda tanpa takut mendapat penilaian buruk. Sebisa mungkin kurangi bahasa sehari-hari yang menguatkan hierarki seperti ",["siap dan mohon izin","https://www.thejakartapost.com/indonesia/2026/07/06/izin-and-siap-military-lingo-creeps-into-civilian-life"]," guna mencegah pendewaan pada figur."]},{"k":"p","s":["Di ruang publik, masyarakat perlu berhenti menjadikan kemarahan pejabat, seremoni berlebihan, atau kedekatan dengan penguasa sebagai ukuran kepemimpinan. Misalnya, kurangi seremonial penyambutan pemimpin yang berlebihan, foto bareng dan cium tangan pejabat, dan ",["mulailah berani untuk mengkritisi kebijakan mereka di forum-forum terbuka","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gW00hnnVNf4"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Dunia akademik juga memiliki tanggung jawab. Pendidikan dan perkuliahan seputar kepemimpinan perlu mengurangi narasi tentang ",["pemimpin sebagai pahlawan tunggal","https://journals.aom.org/doi/abs/10.5465/amle.2014.0079"]," dan lebih banyak membahas kontribusi pekerja, relasi kekuasaan, kondisi sosial yang memengaruhi keberhasilan organisasi hingga ",["dampaknya untuk masyarakat di mana organisasi itu berada","https://journals.aom.org/doi/abs/10.5465/amle.2019.0289"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Post-heroic leadership","https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1048984304000827"]," bukan berarti meniadakan pemimpin. Pendekatan ini menolak anggapan bahwa kekuasaan harus terkonsentrasi pada satu figur yang selalu benar."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kepemimpinan yang sehat bukan ditandai oleh banyaknya orang yang patuh dan bertepuk tangan, melainkan oleh ",["keberanian mereka","https://www.annualreviews.org/content/journals/10.1146/annurev-orgpsych-031413-091328"]," untuk berbeda pendapat tanpa takut kehilangan suara."]}],"chars":6192},"https://theconversation.com/ketidakbecusan-pemerintah-dalam-mengurus-bencana-memengaruhi-narasi-kemerdekaan-di-aceh-292896":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"6cbdc45b0a02f51983425d7f926a5a6c833fd8626875e48c6867e823770e70da","read":"https://theconversation.com/ketidakbecusan-pemerintah-dalam-mengurus-bencana-memengaruhi-narasi-kemerdekaan-di-aceh-292896","bytes":189599,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Ketidakbecusan pemerintah dalam mengurus bencana memengaruhi narasi kemerdekaan di Aceh","by":[{"n":"Azifah Astrina","r":"Ph.D. candidate in Political Science, University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign; Universitas Gadjah Mada"}],"pub":"2026-10-01T06:33:14Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Ribuan orang berkumpul di Masjid Raya Baiturrahman Banda Aceh pada ",["15 Agustus 2026","https://en.tempo.co/read/2117590/aceh-peace-day-tribute-turns-violent-as-crowd-clashes-with-police"]," untuk memperingati ",["21 tahun","https://theacehpost.com/news/bendera-merah-putih-di-pendopo-gubernur-aceh-diturunkan-massa-berkibar-bulan-bintang/index.html"]," perdamaian antara Indonesia dan Gerakan Aceh Merdeka (GAM)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Beberapa peserta mengibarkan bendera bulan bintang berwarna merah, hitam, dan putih sembari meneriakkan “Aceh merdeka.” Sementara peserta lainnya menurunkan bendera merah putih dan menggantinya dengan bendera Aceh."]},{"k":"p","s":["Tindakan ini signifikan secara politik di provinsi tempat konflik bersenjata yang mengupayakan kemerdekaan berlangsung selama hampir ",["tiga dekade","https://media.defense.gov/2025/Apr/07/2003683780/-1/-1/0/20250407_INDONESIA_ACEH_1976-2005%20_FINAL.PDF"]," —sebelum Perjanjian Helsinki 2005 mengakhirinya."]},{"k":"p","s":["Aksi 15 Agustus tersebut bukanlah insiden tunggal. Dalam ulang tahun GAM pada ",["Desember 2024","https://www.thejakartapost.com/indonesia/2024/12/05/gams-crescent-and-star-flag-raised-in-lhoukseumawe"],", mantan anggota GAM juga mengibarkan bendera serupa. Seorang eks kombatan menyuarakan harapan agar bendera itu akhirnya dapat berkibar di seluruh Aceh."]},{"k":"p","s":["Bendera tersebut kemudian meramaikan jalan-jalan di Aceh pada ",["Desember 2025","https://en.tempo.co/read/2076220/tni-disperses-crowds-flying-gam-flags-in-acehs-lhokseumawe"]," sebelum prajurit TNI membubarkan kerumunan yang mengibarkannya."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kembalinya simbol dan slogan ini terjadi saat Aceh berusaha pulih dari banjir parah dan tanah longsor pada akhir ",["November 2025","https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/death-toll-rises-to-164-after-floods-and-landslides-on-indonesias-sumatra-island"],". Padahal, bencana alam yang berbeda, yaitu Tsunami 2004, ",["justru menciptakan kondisi","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.geoforum.2007.10.010"]," yang mempercepat proses perdamaian antara Aceh dan Jakarta."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dua dekade kemudian, ",["kritik","https://news.mongabay.com/2026/06/survivors-sue-indonesian-government-over-response-to-catastrophic-sumatra-floods/"]," terhadap respons pemerintah pusat terhadap penanganan bencana justru memperkuat ekspresi warga Aceh."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sebagai seorang ",["akademisi nasionalisme dan geografi politik","https://pol.illinois.edu/directory/profile/astrina2"],", saya melihat kebangkitan sentimen prokemerdekaan di Aceh bukan sekadar bukti bahwa separatisme sedang kembali."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ia merupakan pengingat bahwa nasionalisme terus-menerus dinegosiasikan antara negara dengan warganya, serta dapat dirusak oleh pengabaian di saat-saat membutuhkan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kesepakatan perdamaian di Aceh yang mengubah konflik separatis berdarah menjadi salah satu contoh ",["rekonsiliasi","https://globalsouthforum.org/article/aceh-at-the-crossroads-hope-for-peace-and-political-challenges-in-a-new-era"]," terbaik di Asia Tenggara. Ketegangan saat ini tidak hanya menimbulkan pertanyaan tentang hubungan Aceh dengan Indonesia, tetapi juga daya tahan perdamaian yang berlangsung lebih dari dua dekade."]},{"k":"h","s":["Perdamaian mengakhiri perang, bukan nasionalisme"]},{"k":"p","s":["Perjuangan GAM sebenarnya melampaui penolakan mereka terhadap kebijakan-kebijakan yang dibuat di Jakarta. Berdiri pada 1976, gerakan ini menampilkan Aceh sebagai bangsa terpisah yang harus merdeka dari Indonesia."]},{"k":"p","s":["GAM mengandalkan sejarah Aceh untuk menggambarkan kemerdekaan ",["sebagai pemulihan","https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.1111/j.1469-8129.2007.00277.x"]," dari kedaulatan ketika Aceh masih menjadi kesultanan independen."]},{"k":"p","s":["Konflik GAM - Indonesia yang berlangsung hampir tiga dekade tersebut ",["menewaskan ribuan orang","https://reliefweb.int/report/indonesia/no-peace-without-justice-victims-indonesia%E2%80%99s-aceh-conflict-demand-truth-justice-and"],". Warga sipil menanggung sebagian besar kekerasan, dengan aparat Indonesia dan GAM sama-sama ",["terlibat dalam pelanggaran","https://www.hrw.org/news/2005/05/27/acehs-forgotten-victims"],". Ini termasuk penyiksaan, penangkapan sewenang-wenang, pemerasan, dan pengungsian paksa."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pada 2004, tsunami dahsyat ",["bertindak sebagai katalis perdamaian","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.geoforum.2007.10.010"],", menyoroti penderitaan populasi Aceh sekaligus membuka pintu bagi bantuan dan kehadiran internasional."]},{"k":"p","s":["Konflik bersenjata secara resmi berakhir dengan penandatanganan ",["Perjanjian Helsinki 2005","https://peacemaker.un.org/sites/default/files/document/files/2024/05/id050815memorandum20of20understanding.pdf"],", tetapi itu tidak membuat nasionalisme Aceh lenyap."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sebaliknya, perdamaian mengakomodasi kekhasan politik Aceh. Perdamaian membuat Aceh memiliki kewenangan pemerintahan sendiri yang luas, mengizinkan partai politik lokal, memperluas representasi politik, dan memberikan daerah tersebut wewenang untuk mengesahkan undang-undang tingkat provinsi."]},{"k":"p","s":["Keleluasaan atas urusan ekonomi dan sumber daya alam diserahkan kepada Aceh, meskipun keluhan yang tersisa mengenai ",["ketentuan bagi hasil terkait ladang gas di sana","https://www.jstor.org/stable/27638587"]," tetap ada hingga hari ini."]},{"k":"p","s":["Penyelesaian politik tersebut sebagian besar berhasil mengakhiri konflik bersenjata. GAM memang melucuti senjatanya. Banyak pula mantan pemimpinnya yang ",["beralih ke","https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/186810341002900105"]," politik pemilu, membentuk partai-partai lokal dan memenangkan posisi-posisi di pemerintahan serta DPR Aceh. Namun, gagasan dan simbol-simbol pro-kemerdekaan tidak sepenuhnya hilang."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pembedaan itu penting karena perdamaian tidak bergantung pada orang Aceh yang meninggalkan identitas politik khas mereka dan menjadi orang Indonesia. Itu bergantung pada pengubahan syarat-syarat hubungan mereka dengan Indonesia."]},{"k":"p","s":["Aceh dapat tetap menjadi bagian dari negara ini sambil mempertahankan kontrol yang besar atas urusan politiknya sendiri. Dalam pengertian itu, Helsinki bukan hanya mengakhiri perang, tetapi juga menciptakan kondisi politik yang membuat Aceh tak berpisah dari Indonesia."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dari bencana menuju pembicaraan kemerdekaan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Banjir dan tanah longsor pada November 2025 menewaskan ",["lebih dari seribu orang","https://thediplomat.com/2025/12/acehs-bitter-lesson-relearned/"]," dan mengakibatkan lebih dari sejuta pengungsi."]},{"k":"p","s":["Aceh termasuk di antara provinsi yang terdampak paling parah, sehingga penduduknya lebih bergantung pada otoritas publik untuk bantuan tanggap darurat dan pemulihan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Desakan agar Presiden menetapkan banjir dan tanah longsor tersebut sebagai ",["bencana nasional","https://www.kompas.id/artikel/en-desakan-penetapan-bencana-nasional-di-sumatera-terus-mengalir-dari-aceh"]," dimulai tak lama setelah bencana menerjang. Namun, Presiden Prabowo Subianto menolaknya karena merasa Indonesia masih mampu."]},{"k":"p","s":["Penolakan Prabowo terhadap bantuan luar negeri menyebabkan ",["kemarahan meluas di Aceh","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/ckgzwqjpzp4o"]," —berbanding terbalik dengan respons Tsunami 2004, ketika bantuan internasional sangat krusial bagi upaya pascabencana."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hampir setahun kemudian, Aceh masih jauh dari pulih. Per 7 September 2026, hanya ",["649 dari 34.777 rumah permanen","https://www.antaranews.com/berita/5730356/satgas-prr-catat-649-unit-hunian-tetap-di-aceh-telah-rampung"]," yang terbangun."]},{"k":"p","s":["Data terbaru yang tersedia juga menunjukkan bahwa 93 ruas jalan daerah masih belum dapat berfungsi. Sementara hanya 188 dari 676 jembatan yang telah dipulihkan per ",["8 Agustus","https://dialeksis.com/aceh/sembilan-bulan-pascabencana-warga-aceh-masih-menunggu-rumah-dan-akses-permanen/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pada ",["14 Agustus,","https://en.tempo.co/read/2117590/aceh-peace-day-tribute-turns-violent-as-crowd-clashes-with-police"]," sehari sebelum acara bendera GAM, koalisi masyarakat sipil kembali mengibarkan bendera putih dan mendesak Jakarta untuk menyatakan bencana tersebut sebagai bencana nasional."]},{"k":"p","s":["Namun mengapa keluhan atas respons pemerintah berubah menjadi pembicaraan prokemerdekaan di Aceh? Sejarah memberikan sebagian jawabannya."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kuatnya identitas Aceh tidak selalu berujung pada aspirasi kemerdekaan. ",["Pemimpin-pemimpin Aceh","https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1469-8129.2007.00277.x"]," yang mendukung kemerdekaan Indonesia dari Belanda pada tahun 1945, dan bahkan ",["pemberontakan Darul Islam","https://media.defense.gov/2024/Mar/20/2003416575/-1/-1/0/20240306_DARULISLAM_1949-62.PDF"]," pada tahun 1950-an, tidak berusaha membentuk negara Aceh yang independen."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sebaliknya, penolakan terhadap pemerintahan kolonial Belanda, yang diikuti oleh jaringan dan solidaritas Islam, ",["justru menghubungkan","https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1469-8129.2007.00277.x"]," elite Aceh dengan komunitas politik Indonesia yang lebih luas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Baru belakangan, ketika hubungan dengan pemerintah pusat memburuk, kemerdekaan menjadi tujuannya."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sejarah ini menunjukkan bahwa nasionalisme Aceh bukanlah kekuatan politik kaku yang secara berkala muncul kembali tanpa perubahan. Pemahaman yang berbeda mengenai bangsa dapat ",["bersaing dan dinegosiasikan ulang","https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1469-8129.2007.00277.x"]," seiring berubahnya kondisi politik."]},{"k":"p","s":["Oleh karena itu, identitas nasional Aceh dan Indonesia tidak selalu saling meniadakan; hubungan keduanya telah berubah seiring berubahnya hubungan politik antara Aceh dan Jakarta."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kembalinya seruan “Aceh Merdeka” dan simbol-simbol terkait GAM menunjukkan bahwa, 21 tahun setelah kesepakatan perdamaian, kemerdekaan menjadi bahasa politik untuk mengekspresikan ketidakpuasan terhadap Indonesia. Ini terutama di momen krusial seperti penanganan bencana yang tak beres sehingga merusak ",["legitimasi pemerintah","https://doi.org/10.1111%2Fgove.12440"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Nasionalisme sebagai proses dua arah"]},{"k":"p","s":["Selama lebih dari dua dekade, Aceh tetap damai dan berada di dalam Indonesia, sambil mempertahankan otonomi yang luas dan identitas politik yang khas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Namun, penggunaan slogan “Aceh Merdeka” dan simbol-simbol separatis menunjukkan bahwa rasa memiliki terhadap Indonesia tidak secara sederhana tuntas oleh perdamaian, otonomi, atau berlalunya waktu."]},{"k":"p","s":["Nasionalisme juga tidak dapat dipahami secara sederhana hanya dengan melihat bagaimana negara-negara membangun identitas melalui ",["sekolah, peta, bendera, dan upacara","https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/epdf/10.1111/nana.70002"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Nasionalisme bekerja dua arah: Indonesia mempromosikan identitas bersama, tetapi orang Aceh juga mencerna apa arti menjadi warga Indonesia melalui interaksi dengan negara."]},{"k":"p","s":["Mungkin pertanyaan yang lebih penting, bukanlah mengapa pembicaraan kemerdekaan kembali muncul, melainkan apa yang telah menjaga Aceh tetap berada di dalam Indonesia selama 21 tahun terakhir."]}],"chars":7932},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/lebanon":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:03Z","sha":"ed882296c21d3888659f5e5d2bf8cf010e28612522cccd8ea48f0064f114c883","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/lebanon","bytes":107641,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Lebanon travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-02-22T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-08-10T14:51:12+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO). Consular support is also severely limited where FCDO advises against travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against travel"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Areas in Beirut and Mount Lebanon Governorate"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to the following areas of Beirut and its southern suburbs, excluding Route 51 from central Beirut to Rafic Hariri International Airport:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Tariq el Jdideh and the area east of Tariq el Jdideh, south of Jalloul Street, west of Hourch and the war cemetery (not including the war cemetery), and south of the Soulieman Bastani"]},{"k":"li","s":["Ghobeiry and the area north of Ghobeiry but south of Yarmouk street, the war cemetery and Horsh park (not including Horsh park and the cemetery and Yarmouk street)"]},{"k":"li","s":["Chiyah (south and west of the Rizkallah Semaan road)"]},{"k":"li","s":["Haret Hraik"]},{"k":"li","s":["Burj Al Barajneh"]},{"k":"li","s":["Mraije"]},{"k":"li","s":["Laylaki"]},{"k":"li","s":["Jnah, south of El Imam Mousa El Sader street"]},{"k":"li","s":["The Golf Club of Lebanon"]},{"k":"li","s":["all other areas west of the Camil Chamoun Boulevard (south of Forn el Chebbak) that becomes the Old Saida Road through Hadath to Beirut airport"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to:"]},{"k":"p","s":["The area of Mount Lebanon Governorate south of (but excluding) the road from Wadi El Zayni in the west (and extending to the Mediterranean Sea), which travels through the villages of Aanout, Gharifeh, Ainbal, Boqaata, Moukhtara, Maaser El Chouf to the Mount Lebanon-Beqaa Governorate boundary in the east"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Areas in the South and Nabatiyeh Governorates"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to South and Nabatiyeh Governorates."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Areas in the Beqaa Governorate"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to:"]},{"k":"p","s":["The area of Beqaa Governorate to the east of (but not including) the Masnaa-Rachaiya Road from Masnaa, Dahr El Ahmar to the Beqaa-Nabatiyeh boundary in the south."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to:"]},{"k":"p","s":["The area of Beqaa Governorate to the south of (but not including) the road from Kafraiya to Joub Jannine, east of (but not including) the road from Joub Jannine to Bar Elias and south of the road from Bar Elias to Deir Zenoun."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Areas in the Baalbek-Hermel Governorate"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to:"]},{"k":"p","s":["The area of Baalbek-Hermel Governorate north of (but not including) the Danniyeh-Hermel Road from the Baalbek-Hermel Governate boundary in the west to Hermel in the east."]},{"k":"p","s":["The area north of (but not including) the Hermel-Ras Baalbek Road from Hermel to the Baalbek-Qaa Highway, and the entire area east of the Baalbek–Qaa Highway (excluding the highway itself), extending south to the Beqaa Governorate boundary."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the rest of the Baalbek-Hermel Governate:"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Areas in the North Governorate"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the area of Tripoli to the east of the Bechara El Khoury road from Bohssas in the south to Beddaoui in the north – including the neighbourhoods of Abou Samra, Tabbaneh, Jessrin, Qoubbeh and Zaytoun."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Areas in the Akkar Governorate"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to:"]},{"k":"p","s":["The area of Akkar Governorate north of (but excluding) the road from Qlayaat in the west (and extending to the Mediterranean Sea) to Tal Keri, Kouaikhat, Aamriyeh, and Qoubaiyat. And east of the same road and from Qoubaiyat to Qatlabah to the boundary of Akkar and Baalbek-Hermel Governorates in the south."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Palestinian refugee camps"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to the 12 Palestinian refugee camps. See ",["Palestinian refugee camp locations","https://www.unrwa.org/where-we-work/lebanon"]," on the UN Relief and Works Agency website."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional tensions"]},{"k":"p","s":["The situation in the Middle East remains unpredictable."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["read ",["If you’re affected by a crisis abroad - GOV.UK","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],". This includes guidance on “how to prepare for a crisis” with suggestions on what you might include in your emergency supplies and “what to do in a crisis”"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow advice from the local authorities"]},{"k":"li","s":["sign up to ",["FCDO Travel Advice email alerts","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information"]},{"k":"li","s":["stay away from areas around security or military facilities"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep your departure plans under review, and ensure your travel documents are up to date"]},{"k":"li","s":["if you are advised to take shelter, stay indoors or find the nearest safe building or designated shelter. An interior stairwell or a room with as few external walls or windows as possible may provide additional protection. The greatest risk is from falling debris caused by intercepts, and you are safest inside a secure structure"]},{"k":"h","s":["Leaving Lebanon"]},{"k":"p","s":["Keep your departure plans under review and ensure your travel documents are up to date, including any visas required for onward travel. Make sure you have access to emergency supplies and essential medication. Travel to or within Lebanon is at your own risk. and you should have a personal emergency plan which does not rely on the UK government."]},{"k":"h","s":["Conflict affecting Lebanon"]},{"k":"p","s":["Since 2 March, conflict in Lebanon escalated in response to regional events. Airstrikes and rocket attacks between Israel and Lebanese Hizballah increased. Widespread evacuation warnings led to a mass movement of people from conflict-affected areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Israeli airstrikes have occurred primarily in the South, Nabatieh and Beqaa Governates and Beirut’s southern suburbs, but have also occurred outside these areas. The Israeli military often releases evacuation warnings before airstrikes, but many have also taken place with no advance notice."]},{"k":"p","s":["A cessation of hostilities was announced in June 2026 but fighting and airstrikes have continued particularly in southern Lebanon, where an Israeli military presence remains. The dynamic nature of the conflict means the situation may change quickly. British nationals should follow local, international and social media to keep up to date with official alerts."]},{"k":"p","s":["We advise you to keep up to date with the latest situation, including using multiple media sources to understand frequency and location of strikes, as these may change rapidly. There are various mapping sources available online."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Access to Beirut airport"]},{"k":"p","s":["Beirut airport is open and operational. If you are travelling to the airport, check the local security situation before you travel. Remain alert to local conditions as these could change quickly."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Civil disorder"]},{"k":"p","s":["Celebratory gunfire is common in Lebanon and there is a risk from gunfire being fired in residential areas in reaction to major regional developments. If you hear gunfire, take cover immediately. Protests related to regional events could also take place at short notice and may escalate quickly. Exercise caution, avoid demonstrations, and monitor local media for developments."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Local support"]},{"k":"p","s":["Our embassy is operating as normal."]},{"k":"p","s":["Keep up to date with local and international media including TV and radio stations such as Virgin Radio Lebanon (FM 89.5) and Voice of Lebanon / Sawt Lubnan (FM 100.3 - 100.5) which may be useful sources of information on any developments."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should have a personal emergency plan that does not rely on the UK government. This may include the ability to leave quickly or to shelter in place if you judge it necessary and safe to do so."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read FCDO advice on what to do ",["if you’re affected by a crisis abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"]," and how to prepare."]},{"k":"h","s":["Help and support in Lebanon"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can contact the emergency services by calling 112."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you need urgent help (for example, you’ve been attacked, arrested or someone has died), call +961 (0)1 960 800."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/lebanon/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK who choose to travel against FCDO advice. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Lebanon’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Lebanon set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Lebanese Embassy in the UK","https://www.lebanon-embassy.org/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your passport should be valid for at least 3 months from the date you enter Lebanon."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document, or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Checks at border control"]},{"k":"p","s":["If your passport contains an Israeli stamp, you may be refused entry to Lebanon even if you hold a valid Lebanese visa."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["British citizens can normally apply for a free single-entry tourist or family visit visa on arrival at Beirut airport. A tourist visa is valid for one month from the date of entry. Travellers can extend their visa for up to three months at the General Security offices."]},{"k":"p","s":["British citizens can also obtain a visa from the Lebanese Embassy in London. These may be valid for a different time period. Travellers should make sure they understand their visa validity to avoid any penalties for overstaying."]},{"k":"p","s":["Travellers overstaying their visa may have to pay a fine at the airport. Only Lebanese currency will be accepted for payment. This should be paid at departures before security procedures."]},{"k":"p","s":["Entry requirements may change at short notice. Check with the ",["Lebanese Embassy","https://www.lebanon-embassy.org/"]," in the UK before you travel."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Name checks against offender database"]},{"k":"p","s":["Lebanese immigration authorities check all visitors’ names on arrival against a database of those wanted for, or convicted of, offences in Lebanon. If your name matches an entry on the database, you may be detained (or occasionally allowed entry by surrendering your passport) until they can be satisfied that the record does not relate to you. You might be able to do this by producing a copy of a birth certificate or other official documentation that allows parents’ names to be checked against the database. Consider carrying this kind of supporting documentation."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Lebanon guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/126/lebanon#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Lebanon"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are likely to try to carry out attacks in Lebanon."]},{"k":"p","s":["Islamist terrorist groups seek to target the Lebanese state, security services, and civilians, and intend to target foreigners in Lebanon. Groups within Lebanon, including Lebanese Hizballah, are proscribed under the Terrorism Act 2000 and the Counter Terrorism (Sanctions) (EU Exit) Regulations 2019. Offences committed under the act – including funding and supporting proscribed organisations – may be liable to prosecution in the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist groups have particularly operated in:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Tripoli"]},{"k":"li","s":["Palestinian refugee camps"]},{"k":"li","s":["areas close to the Syrian border, including around Hermel and Aarsal"]},{"k":"li","s":["Southern suburbs of Beirut"]},{"k":"p","s":["Recent terrorist-related incidents include a firearm attack which targeted the US embassy in 2024:"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a heightened risk of terrorism against aviation. Additional security measures have been in place on flights departing from Lebanon to the UK since March 2017. You should co-operate fully with security officials."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you notice or suspect a security incident is underway, leave the area immediately. Suspects have detonated explosives to avoid arrest. Keep clear of affected areas immediately after any attacks."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorist kidnap"]},{"k":"p","s":["There’s a threat of kidnapping in Lebanon. The Lebanese authorities have warned that foreigners could be targeted."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals are seen as legitimate targets, including tourists, humanitarian aid workers, journalists and business travellers. If you are kidnapped, the reason for your presence is unlikely to protect you or secure your safe release."]},{"k":"p","s":["The long-standing policy of the British Government is not to make substantive concessions to hostage takers. The British Government considers that paying ransoms and releasing prisoners builds the capability of terrorist groups and finances their activities. This can, in turn, increase the risk of further hostage-taking. The Terrorism Act (2000) makes payments to terrorists illegal."]},{"k":"h","s":["Security situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["The security situation in Lebanon is volatile and can deteriorate quickly."]},{"k":"p","s":["Violence may occur:"]},{"k":"li","s":["as a result of the ",["conflict affecting Lebanon","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/lebanon#conflict-in-neighbouring-israel-and-the-occupied-palestinian-territories-opts"]]},{"k":"li","s":["between security forces and protestors"]},{"k":"li","s":["between supporters of political groups"]},{"k":"li","s":["over scarce or subsidised resources"]},{"k":"p","s":["Confrontations often happen without warning and can result in large numbers of casualties. Security forces may use tear gas and rubber bullets during clashes."]},{"k":"p","s":["Weapons are common in Lebanon and groups such as Lebanese Hizballah have arms that are beyond state control. Arguments can quickly escalate into violence, including the use of weapons, typically firearms and bladed weapons."]},{"k":"p","s":["Celebratory gunfire is illegal in Lebanon but remains widespread. Every year there are reported casualties."]},{"k":"p","s":["Regional and international developments such as in Iran, Israel, Syria and Iraq can have an impact on the local security situation. Monitor the regional situation whilst in Lebanon."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Security advice for British nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid large crowds and political gatherings"]},{"k":"li","s":["take cover in a building and move away from windows in areas where there’s celebratory or other gunfire"]},{"k":"li","s":["be especially vigilant during periods of religious significance (including the holy month of Ramadan) and public holidays"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor this travel advice and ",["sign up for email updates","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/lebanon/email-signup"]]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure you have correct and up-to-date travel documents, including a ",["passport","https://www.gov.uk/overseas-passports"]," and ",["visa","https://www.gov.uk/apply-to-come-to-the-uk"]," if necessary, for yourself and anyone you are travelling with (even if they are not a British national) in case a sudden deterioration in the security situation means you need to leave Lebanon"]},{"k":"p","s":["If there are widespread disturbances or the security situation deteriorates, there may be limits to the assistance that the British Embassy Beirut can provide. Be prepared to shelter in place for several days, if the security situation requires it. This means having enough essential supplies, such as food, water and medicine, at the place where you are staying. Do not rely on the FCDO being able to evacuate you in an emergency."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read FCDO advice on what to do ",["if you’re affected by a crisis abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"]," and how to prepare."]},{"k":"h","s":["Severe economic crisis"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Currency"]},{"k":"p","s":["Lebanon is experiencing a prolonged economic crisis. This may affect your ability to pay for goods and services by credit or debit card. US dollars are widely accepted and are the main cash currency, including in most supermarkets, restaurants and other retail outlets. It may be difficult or expensive to access US dollars locally and many companies do not accept credit/debit cards. Plan accordingly and ensure you have access to adequate cash for the length of your stay."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Power cuts"]},{"k":"p","s":["Lebanon’s power plants are only producing limited electricity for the national grid. This can lead to power cuts. Many businesses rely heavily on generators for electricity, and electricity provision can vary. Have a torch to hand at night and plan how you would leave your accommodation in the dark."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is moderate risk to tourists from petty or violent crime. Take sensible precautions to protect yourself and your belongings:"]},{"k":"li","s":["consider your route and vary daily routines"]},{"k":"li","s":["hide expensive-looking jewellery, which could draw unwanted attention"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid carrying large amounts of cash in public"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware of your surroundings when using ATMs"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sexual assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been reported incidents of sexual harassment and assault in public areas. Consider whether it is safe to walk alone, particularly in less busy areas. Due to the lack of electricity, streetlights often do not work, so streets can be dark at night. Consider taking a torch with you at night and make sure your phone is charged in case of an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drug smuggling and violent crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Criminal gangs involved in drug cultivation and smuggling operate in parts of the Beqaa Valley, especially northern Beqaa. Other armed crimes, such as robbery and kidnap, can occur in these areas. There are also frequent armed clashes between gangs and the security forces."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras and drones in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid photography in Lebanese Hizballah areas, including the southern suburbs of Beirut, the Beqaa Valley and areas in southern Lebanon. You may be detained if you are observed taking photographs."]},{"k":"p","s":["Only take photographs in tourist sites. You could be arrested for photographing military sites. Flying drone cameras without permission is illegal."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ramadan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ramadan is a holy month for Muslims. The dates vary by year and country. During this time, be aware of:"]},{"k":"li","s":["eating, drinking, smoking or chewing gum in public in the daytime, including in your car"]},{"k":"li","s":["playing loud music or dance"]},{"k":"li","s":["swearing in public"]},{"k":"p","s":["Get more advice when you arrive from your tour guide, hotel or business contacts."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check opening hours of shops and restaurants"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow local dress codes – clothing that does not meet local dress codes may cause more offence at this time"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Diversity"]},{"k":"p","s":["Lebanon’s people are diverse, with many different Muslim and Christian sects represented. Respect local traditions, customs, laws and religions at all times and make sure your actions do not offend."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dress code"]},{"k":"p","s":["In many areas you will find dress codes more relaxed than in other countries of the region, but you should still dress modestly when visiting religious sites."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Possessing, using and trafficking illegal drugs (including small quantities) are all serious offences, punishable with prison sentences."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Lebanese Criminal Code includes a general provision concerning ‘every sexual act against nature’. Lebanese courts might consider that this includes same sex sexual activity. A criminal offence under this provision is punishable by a prison sentence of up to a year. The ",["Lebanese Medical Association for Sexual Health","https://lebmash.org/resources-for-lgbt-individuals/"]," has resources for LGBT+ people."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Child abduction and travel bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have concerns about child custody, ",["get legal advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/child-abduction-accredited-solicitors-referral-list"]," before travelling to Lebanon about ‘travel bans’ that can be imposed by male heads of family. Even if you or your child holds a British passport you may be subject to Lebanese laws and regulations."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Lebanon a father or husband can legally arrange for a travel ban to be placed on their wife or children. If a travel ban is placed on you or your children, you will not be able to travel. If that does happen a parent should seek ",["legal assistance","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers/Lebanon/result?"]," to check if the travel ban can be lifted."]},{"k":"p","s":["Lebanese family law is very different from UK law and particular care is needed if child custody becomes an issue."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re a British national involved in international parental child abductions or custody disputes, ",["contact the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)","https://www.gov.uk/government/collections/support-for-british-nationals-abroad"]," for assistance or call +44 (0) 2070 085 000. FCDO has information on international parental child abduction, including how we can help. FCDO strongly advises against attempting to move your child yourself. This may be considered abduction (or ‘re-abduction’). This may be illegal and can put your child at risk."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Shared taxis and unofficial taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not use shared taxis or taxis hailed on the street. In 2017, the Lebanese Interior Minister advised people in Lebanon not to use Uber taxis."]},{"k":"p","s":["Only use taxis:"]},{"k":"li","s":["from recognised companies that use vetted drivers"]},{"k":"li","s":["recognised by hotels, which are safe and well-maintained"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been armed robberies and physical attacks against passengers in shared taxis (known locally as service taxis) with passengers being attacked by either the driver or other passengers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["You need either a 1968 ",["international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," or a UK driving licence to drive in Lebanon. The 1949 IDP is not accepted anymore. You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Lebanon, see information on ",["driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving standards are poor and the accident rate is high. Traffic lights are often switched off and not always observed. It may be better to hire a car with a driver if you’re inexperienced. You must wear a seat belt (if fitted). Avoid travelling at night outside towns if possible. Cars with diesel engines are banned."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Licences and permits"]},{"k":"p","s":["Carry ID with you at all times and be prepared to stop at checkpoints to show your papers. The army has set up checkpoints on major and minor roads."]},{"k":"p","s":["Temporary local licences are also available, but they take longer to get and are more expensive than an IDP."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Roadblocks"]},{"k":"p","s":["Protests and roadblocks may restrict travel at short notice. Major roads in and out of Beirut and across the country, including the roads to and from Beirut Rafik Hariri International Airport, have become blocked at short notice. If you’re travelling to or from the airport, check your flight status before leaving and allow extra time for your journey. If roads from the airport are blocked, wait there until the authorities confirm access roads are open."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Landmines"]},{"k":"p","s":["Landmines and other unexploded weapons are present in Lebanon and are not always clearly marked. Use only well-travelled tracks and do not stray from their edges. Avoid remote abandoned properties. Use local guides and seek local knowledge if you are unsure."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Forest fires"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a heightened risk of forest fires in Lebanon, particularly during summer. Forest fires are highly dangerous and unpredictable. Take care when visiting or driving through woodland areas. The authorities may evacuate areas and close roads for safety."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are travelling in Lebanon, familiarise yourself with local safety and emergency procedures, stay vigilant, and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["For information on the risk of forest fires, visit the Disaster Risk Management website, ",["Facebook page","https://www.facebook.com/drmleb/"]," and ",["X account","https://x.com/DRM_Lebanon"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you see a forest fire, call the emergency services on 112 (for the fire service, call 175)."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Lebanon is in an earthquake zone. There have been no damaging tremors in recent years, although Lebanon experienced strong aftershocks from an earthquake in Turkey in February 2023. The US Federal Emergency Management Agency has advice about what to do before, during and after an earthquake."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Lebanon. It only covers regions where FCDO has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/lebanon/warnings-and-insurance"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/lebanon/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Southern suburbs of Beirut"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to the southern suburbs of Beirut due to the presence of armed groups and heightened risk of organised crime including kidnapping."]},{"k":"p","s":["Weapons are common in these areas and groups such as Lebanese Hizballah have arms that are beyond state control. There have been Israeli airstrikes in the southern suburbs of Beirut in 2026. Future airstrikes cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas in the South and Nabatiyeh Governorates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Since 2023, there has been frequent artillery fire and airstrikes in Lebanon, particularly in the South and Nabatiyeh Governorates. There is a risk of further strikes in the area."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a UN peacekeeping presence in the area south of the Litani River due to tensions between Lebanon and Israel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Israeli Defence Forces currently retain a presence in southern Lebanon . British Nationals should be aware that Israeli Defences Forces have fired at civilians who have ignored their instructions to leave these areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["Conflict affecting Lebanon","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/lebanon#conflict-affecting-Lebanon"]," for further information."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas in the Beqaa Governorate, including the Beqaa Valley"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel and all but essential travel to areas in the Beqaa Governorate (as described in ‘Warnings and insurance’ page) due to risks from Israeli airstrikes and criminal activity in these areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Since 2024, there have been several Israeli airstrikes in the Beqaa Valley. There is a risk of further strikes in the area."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas in the Baalbek-Hermel Governorate"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have also been Israeli airstrikes in Baalbek-Hermel Governorate, including the town of Baalbek."]},{"k":"p","s":["In addition, British nationals should be vigilant to heightened risks from criminal activity in the Baalbek-Hermel Governorate. Since 2025, there have been several instances of deadly armed clashes between Lebanese and Syrian groups in border towns near Hermel. Further clashes cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Lebanese Armed Forces have conducted raids against narcotics factories in Baalbek, resulting in the death of numerous soldiers. Since 2024, there have been airstrikes close to the highway and near to the border with Syria. Further strikes cannot be ruled out in this area."]},{"k":"h","s":["Palestinian refugee camps"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to the 12 Palestinian refugee camps. See ",["Palestinian refugee camp locations","https://www.unrwa.org/where-we-work/lebanon"]," on the UN Relief and Works Agency website."]},{"k":"p","s":["Palestinian refugee camps are volatile environments where the Lebanese state has limited capacity to impose law and order. There has been a long pattern of violent clashes."]},{"k":"p","s":["In September 2023, Ain el Hilweh camp witnessed intense violence resulting in a number of casualties. There were reports of bullets reaching as far as Ghaziyeh Town (2km south). The situation remains volatile and tensions could escalate without warning. There have been Israeli airstrikes on Palestinian refugee camps, including strikes on Ain el Hilweh camp in November 2025, February 2026 and March 2026, which resulted in casualties."]},{"k":"h","s":["Akkar Governorate including the city of Tripoli"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to the area of Akkar Governate close to the Syrian border due to the unstable security situation in Syria."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to some areas of the city of Tripoli due to the risk of criminality, localised armed disputes, and public disorder."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 140 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Lebanon","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/126/lebanon#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Lebanon","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/126/lebanon"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been reported cases of cholera in Lebanon. More guidance is available in ",["TravelHealthPro’s cholera factsheet","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/56/cholera"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical supplies can occasionally be hard to find in country. Take any medicines you need with you to Lebanon. The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or purchased in the UK can be different in other countries. If you’re travelling with prescription medication you should carry a medical certificate confirming that the medication has been prescribed for a medical condition."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Lebanon"]},{"k":"p","s":["The availability and quality of medical treatment available in Lebanon has been affected by the economic crisis and fuel shortages, although the situation has stabilised for private healthcare/hospitals in Beirut."]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical care in Lebanon can be expensive. Most medical providers and hospitals are insisting on significant cash deposits before admitting patients, including in emergency situations. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["Doctors are generally well qualified, though nursing standards vary. Most medical staff speak French and English."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Lebanon","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/lebanon-doctors/list-of-medical-facilities-in-lebanon"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Lebanon"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 140"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 175"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 112"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Lebanon"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Lebanon"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=lebanon"]," in Lebanon"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Lebanon","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/lebanon-bereavement-support"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being arrested or ",["imprisoned in Lebanon","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/lebanon-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/lebanon/british-embassy-beirut"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/lebanon/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Lebanon","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-lebanon"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":30627,"change":"FCDO has changed the areas of Lebanon where it advises against all travel or all but essential travel. FCDO no longer advises against all travel or all but essential travel to some parts of Lebanon. FCDO continues to advise against all travel and all but essential travel to other areas of Lebanon."},"https://theconversation.com/republican-gerrymandering-worked-pretty-well-in-texas-and-florida-even-if-it-backfired-in-north-carolina-and-ohio-295944":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:32Z","sha":"4dfd440074b94dfb997e5d452b40a10ff439a4896332da4db2c53367b7740ca9","read":"https://theconversation.com/republican-gerrymandering-worked-pretty-well-in-texas-and-florida-even-if-it-backfired-in-north-carolina-and-ohio-295944","bytes":186211,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Republican gerrymandering worked pretty well in Texas and Florida, even if it backfired in North Carolina and Ohio","by":[{"n":"Charlie Hunt","r":"Associate Professor of Political Science, Boise State University"}],"pub":"2026-11-13T13:37:40Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["During the 2026 election cycle, ",["Republicans enacted a series of gerrymanders","https://www.ncsl.org/redistricting-and-census/changing-the-maps-tracking-mid-decade-redistricting"]," – a form of partisan redistricting – in a handful of states to give them a disproportionate edge over Democrats in their congressional delegations. Democrats responded with a ",["successful redistricting effort in California","https://www.scotusblog.com/2026/02/supreme-court-allows-california-to-use-congressional-map-benefitting-democrats/"]," and an ",["unsuccessful one in Virginia","https://www.npr.org/2026/05/08/nx-s1-5805193/redistricting-virginia-trump-midterms"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Gerrymandering has obvious implications for fairness and democracy, characterized by some as politicians picking their voters, not voters picking their politicians."]},{"k":"p","s":["There’s also a practical consideration for those doing the gerrymandering: The efforts can fail when they overplay their hand."]},{"k":"p","s":["By spreading their supportive voters across many districts, parties can create more seats that may lean in their direction. But if spread too thin, ",["these efforts can backfire","https://theconversation.com/3-reasons-republicans-redistricting-power-grab-might-backfire-262553"]," and net seats for the other party, particularly in a “wave” election year that favors the other party. This unintended consequence is ",["often referred to as a “dummymander","https://sites.socsci.uci.edu/%7Ebgrofman/140%20Grofman%20and%20Brunell.%20%202005%20%20The%20Art%20of%20the%20Dummymander....pdf"],".”"]},{"k":"p","s":["So, with such massive Democratic majorities poised to enter the 120th Congress, did Republican attempts to gerrymander actually end up costing them some seats in the U.S. House?"]},{"k":"p","s":["The answer isn’t as clear-cut as you might think."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dummymanders in North Carolina and Ohio?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Republican state legislatures in Ohio and North Carolina ",["redrew their congressional maps in 2025","https://www.ncsl.org/redistricting-and-census/changing-the-maps-tracking-mid-decade-redistricting"],", crafting a set of districts they believed would maximize the number of seats they could win in the House."]},{"k":"p","s":["Despite both states being traditionally competitive in statewide elections, their state legislatures drew a collection of seats Republicans believed they would win: 12 of these 15 new seats in Ohio and 11 out of 14 in North Carolina included a majority of voters who voted for Donald Trump in the 2024 presidential election."]},{"k":"p","s":["But in 2026, Democrats across the country ",["won dozens of seats","https://www.cbsnews.com/news/house-districts-flipped-2026-midterm-elections/"]," that had previously seemed out of reach, including districts Trump won by double digits in 2024. Many of these seats were in heavily gerrymandered Republican seats."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Ohio and North Carolina, the size and scope of the midterm backlash against Trump and his party put many of the seats Republicans targeted in these states, including ones Trump won by as many as 20 points, in serious jeopardy."]},{"k":"p","s":["In the end, the Democratic wave overcame so many Trump-won seats in these states that their new delegations to Congress may be more Democratic than they would have been without the gerrymanders."]},{"k":"h","s":["Democrats held the line in the deep South"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Texas and Florida also targeted a series of Democrat-held seats","https://www.npr.org/2026/11/04/nx-s1-6028588/redistricting-efforts-failed-republicans"]," to flip their way in 2026. Nine such seats across these two states, as well as a vulnerable seat held by Democratic U.S. Rep. Shomari Figures in Alabama, were the targets of gerrymanders that created new districts that Trump won in 2024, all by 9 percentage points or more."]},{"k":"p","s":["But once the 2026 Democratic wave swept through the deep South, these gerrymanders were essentially canceled out. Despite the gains the party projected, Republicans in these three states appear likely to enter the 120th Congress with delegations the same size as they had in the 119th."]},{"k":"p","s":["Other Republican gerrymandering attempts were successful, but only barely. In Tennessee’s 9th District, the last remaining Democratic seat in the state ",["was gerrymandered","https://sos.tn.gov/announcements/2026-congressional-redistricting"]," into a district Donald Trump won by 21 points in 2024. Republicans did ",["hold that seat","https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2026/11/03/us/elections/results-tennessee-us-house-9.html"]," as expected, but only by 2,500 votes, or just over 1 percentage point."]},{"k":"h","s":["Gerrymanders that worked – and didn’t"]},{"k":"p","s":["Many of these gerrymanders were not maximally successful. But were they true dummymanders?"]},{"k":"p","s":["In North Carolina and Ohio it does appear that Republicans overplayed their hand by counting on past Trump voters in a national environment that proved so favorable to the Democrats."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Ohio, a gerrymander that aimed for a two-thirds Republican majority in their House delegation will net them ",["less than half of that in the 120th Congress","https://www.wosu.org/politics-government/2026-11-04/ohio-democrats-overcome-congressional-gerrymandering-likely-flipping-three-seats"],". That outcome ended up producing a more representative result, one that was roughly in line with the two parties’ 2026 popular vote shares in the state."]},{"k":"p","s":["North Carolina was a more drastic dummymander: The Republicans aimed to design districts where they would win seats accounting for almost two-thirds of their congressional delegation. But the party is ",["currently poised to hold","https://carolinapublicpress.org/82900/gop-gerrymander-backfires-in-nc-as-states-congressional-map-goes-blue/"],", at best, less than one-third of their state’s seats."]},{"k":"p","s":["And California, which Democrats gerrymandered in reaction to Republican efforts in other states, is ",["a partisan success story","https://calmatters.org/newsletter/california-midterm-gerrymander/"],". The state is projected to send only 8% of their delegation to the House as Republicans, despite voting 30% for Republicans statewide."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Texas and Florida the story is more complicated. Democrats in those states retained most of the seats they held that their Republican legislatures targeted in their gerrymanders, thanks to ",["historic shifts by Hispanic voters","https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/latino-voters-propel-democrats-to-big-wins-with-leftward-swing"]," who had voted for Trump in the 2024 election."]},{"k":"p","s":["But gerrymanders can be effective beyond marginal, targeted districts. Taken as a whole, Texas’ and Florida’s district boundaries were drawn so favorably for Republicans that even a Democratic tsunami managed only to keep these states’ delegations identical in the next Congress, since many other districts remained safe for Republicans."]},{"k":"p","s":["In these states, Republicans still enjoy a greater proportion of House seats than their popular vote margins would reflect. And in a less Democrat-leaning election cycle, many of these gerrymandered seats could very well shift back toward Republicans."]},{"k":"h","s":["Failed GOP gerrymanders would have produced an even bigger blue wave"]},{"k":"p","s":["As poor as the outcome of the 2026 midterms was for Republicans, it could have been even worse. In fact, some Republican states might count themselves lucky that their attempts to gerrymander failed in the lead-up to the midterms."]},{"k":"p","s":["In traditionally Republican states such as ",["Missouri","https://statecourtreport.org/our-work/analysis-opinion/chaos-missouris-redistricting-litigation"]," and ",["Utah","https://redistricting.lls.edu/case/lwv-of-utah-v-utah-state-legislature/"],", courts struck down gerrymanders that would have created a series of districts that ",["Trump won","https://ballotpedia.org/Redistricting_in_Missouri_ahead_of_the_2026_elections"]," by around ",["20 percentage points","https://ballotpedia.org/Redistricting_in_Utah_ahead_of_the_2026_elections"],". If the gerrymanders had not been struck down, Democrats’ shocking success in similar districts across the country could have netted them as many as five additional seats in these states."]},{"k":"p","s":["A similar situation played out in ",["Indiana","https://www.cbsnews.com/news/indiana-redistricting-vote-fails-senate-trump/"]," and ",["South Carolina","https://www.npr.org/2026/05/26/nx-s1-5831996/redistricting-midterms-trump-south-carolina"],". New maps pushed by Trump that failed in their state legislatures were intended to produce even more lopsided Republican gains. But ",["analysis from the Cook Political Report","https://www.cookpolitical.com/analysis/house/house-overview/could-blue-wave-drown-out-mid-decade-redistricting"]," found that these maps might have netted Democrats as many as six out of South Carolina’s seven House seats, and eight out of Indiana’s nine. Instead, Democrats seem likely to end up with only a pair of seats in each state."]},{"k":"h","s":["What’s next in gerrymandering wars?"]},{"k":"p","s":["The 2026 election cycle demonstrates that gerrymandering is a far more complex and dynamic proposition than it is often treated by pundits and parties."]},{"k":"p","s":["Wave elections of this size can often overcome the intended effects of gerrymandered maps, but subsequent elections might find them much more effective. Plus, parties often draw gerrymandered maps based on the previous election’s presidential results – a measure that may be less reliable as voters continue to make more unexpected choices."]},{"k":"p","s":["Moreover, both red and blue states are dealing with the aftermath of the ",["Louisiana v. Callais Supreme Court decision","https://constitutioncenter.org/blog/the-supreme-courts-callais-decision-sets-new-framework-for-racial-gerrymandering"],", which made the gerrymandering of racial groups easier to do without court interventions. Over the next two years, Republicans may attempt to implement even more new maps in many new states, particularly in the South. Those new districts will likely aim to dilute ",["majority-Black districts","https://www.hks.harvard.edu/faculty-research/policy-topics/fairness-justice/what-louisiana-v-callais-means-voting-rights-act"]," that are no longer protected by the Voting Rights Act."]},{"k":"p","s":["Meanwhile, Democratic state governments ",["appear poised to continue","https://www.thebulwark.com/p/democrat-not-backing-off-their-own-redistricting-push-after-2026-midterms"]," with their pushback against last cycle’s Republican efforts with gerrymanders of their own over the next two years."]},{"k":"p","s":["But the Republican redistricting failures of the 2026 cycle, including their near misses, should make both parties cautious about future attempts."]}],"chars":7855},"https://theconversation.com/young-black-men-in-philly-are-more-likely-to-be-pulled-over-if-driving-with-friends-study-shows-295735":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:32Z","sha":"e1b6945a508a52ebdcdc05c4af0d9eeb60115a33195428aed0da8aee366fe652","read":"https://theconversation.com/young-black-men-in-philly-are-more-likely-to-be-pulled-over-if-driving-with-friends-study-shows-295735","bytes":178569,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Young Black men in Philly are more likely to be pulled over if driving with friends, study shows","by":[{"n":"Lance Hannon","r":"Professor of Sociology and Criminology, Villanova University"}],"pub":"2026-11-09T13:41:26Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Deciding whether to drive somewhere alone or with friends is typically a matter of convenience or personal preference. But for young Black men in Philadelphia, that decision may carry an additional consideration: the likelihood of being pulled over by police."]},{"k":"p","s":["My recent co-authored research suggests that young Black men traveling together ",["attract significantly more police scrutiny","https://doi.org/10.1007/s12552-026-09530-z"]," than those driving alone."]},{"k":"p","s":["In fact, the apparent effect of traveling with another young Black man was larger than the racial disparity detected when comparing young Black and white male drivers."]},{"k":"p","s":["These findings challenge a common assumption about racial profiling: that its defining feature is simply whether a driver is Black or white."]},{"k":"h","s":["What 41,633 traffic stops reveal"]},{"k":"p","s":["As a ",["criminologist","https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=ZfzwxMgAAAAJ&hl=en&oi=ao"],", I have published numerous peer-reviewed articles on police stops. I recently published a study on this topic in the journal Race and Social Problems with Molly Biddle, who at the time of writing was a ",["data analyst","https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Molly-Biddle-3"]," for the Police Accountability Unit at the Defender Association of Philadelphia. In that study, ",["we analyzed Philadelphia Police Department traffic stop records","https://doi.org/10.1007/s12552-026-09530-z"]," from 2021 through 2024."]},{"k":"p","s":["We focused on men ages 18-29 stopped for motor vehicle code violations that did not involve an arrest. Among young Black males, approximately 1 in 4 were investigated alongside another young Black man in the car. Among young white males, less than 1 in 20 were investigated with another young white man."]},{"k":"p","s":["This fivefold disparity is striking, but it does not necessarily establish discriminatory policing. Different groups might have different driving habits or preferences for traveling together."]},{"k":"p","s":["To investigate whether police decisions contributed to this disparity, we employed a statistical technique known as the ",["“veil-of-darkness” test","https://www.jstor.org/stable/27590768"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["What changes when the Sun goes down?"]},{"k":"p","s":["The veil-of-darkness test takes advantage of the fact that sunset occurs at different times throughout the year."]},{"k":"p","s":["For example, an officer may be able to clearly see a vehicle’s occupants from a distance at 7 p.m. during summer but have a much more obscured view at the same hour during winter. Importantly, the idea is that daylight visibility can help an officer distinguish who is in the vehicle before the decision is made to pull the car over."]},{"k":"p","s":["By comparing stops occurring at similar times under different lighting conditions, researchers can investigate whether the ability to distinguish vehicle occupants from afar influences traffic enforcement."]},{"k":"p","s":["Our results revealed two important patterns."]},{"k":"p","s":["First, the disparity between young Black men stopped and young white men stopped decreased when it was harder to see who is in the car. This is consistent with ",["what other researchers have found","https://openpolicing.stanford.edu/tutorials/"]," using earlier data for Philadelphia."]},{"k":"p","s":["Second, and this is what makes our analysis novel, we found that obscured visibility had an even greater impact on reducing the gap between young Black males stopped in groups versus driving alone."]},{"k":"p","s":["Both patterns were statistically significant, even after accounting for time of day, neighborhood, police assignment, season and other factors."]},{"k":"p","s":["These findings suggest that the visibility of a young Black male passenger in a vehicle may influence police decisions as much or even more than the visibility of a driver’s race alone."]},{"k":"p","s":["Social psychological research offers a possible explanation for our results. People sometimes perceive groups as more threatening than individuals, and ",["racial stereotypes can intensify those perceptions","https://doi.org/10.1177/1948550619876638"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Two young Black men together may therefore be perceived as much more suspicious than either would be individually."]},{"k":"p","s":["Indeed, in our sample, young Black male drivers investigated with young Black male passengers were far more likely to be pulled out of the vehicle and fruitlessly frisked for contraband than to receive a citation for the traffic offense used to justify the encounter in the first place. Only 7% were ticketed, which suggests that many stops were pretextual."]},{"k":"h","s":["Racial profiling isn’t just about the driver’s race"]},{"k":"p","s":["Our recent findings build on our earlier study that examined more than 76,000 traffic stops involving ",["Black drivers in predominantly Black Philadelphia neighborhoods","https://doi.org/10.1007/s12103-025-09879-8"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["That research found that the proportional representation of younger Black men among stopped drivers increased with daylight visibility, while the proportional representation of older Black women decreased."]},{"k":"p","s":["The estimated magnitude of this within-race disparity was comparable to estimates commonly reported in studies comparing stops of Black versus white motorists."]},{"k":"p","s":["Together, our two studies reveal that unfair differences in police scrutiny within the Black population can be as large as, or larger than, disparities detected through conventional Black-white comparisons."]},{"k":"p","s":["Beyond investigating the extent to which the police pull over a greater quantity of Black drivers than white drivers, our research points to the need for police accountability advocates to ask additional questions about passengers and intraracial disparities."]},{"k":"p","s":["For example, when policing in virtually all-Black communities, are some officers more blind to a driver’s age and gender than others? Likewise, are certain officers more likely to pull over young Black men when they are seen traveling in groups?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Such questions call attention to the idea that fairness within communities is just as important as fairness between them."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more of our stories about ",["Philadelphia and Pennsylvania","https://theconversation.com/us/philadelphia-pennsylvania-news"],", or sign up for our Philadelphia ",["newsletter on Substack","https://tcphilly.substack.com/"],"."]}],"chars":5488},"https://theconversation.com/a-seismic-icj-ruling-has-found-myanmar-responsible-for-genocide-but-will-it-help-the-rohingya-296700":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-20T01:14Z","sha":"d86ef1222cebfd14c244ee158c7749d0585051f139d6effd908e63a2ea328d35","read":"https://theconversation.com/a-seismic-icj-ruling-has-found-myanmar-responsible-for-genocide-but-will-it-help-the-rohingya-296700","bytes":184425,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"A seismic ICJ ruling has found Myanmar responsible for genocide. But will it help the Rohingya?","by":[{"n":"Juliette McIntyre","r":"Senior Lecturer in Law, Adelaide University"},{"n":"Adam Simpson","r":"Senior Lecturer in International Studies in the School of Society and Culture, Adelaide University"}],"pub":"2026-11-20T00:35:00Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Yesterday, the ",["International Court of Justice","https://www.icj-cij.org/case/178"]," in The Hague ",["ruled","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/19/what-the-icj-ruling-means-for-the-rohingya"],", by nine votes to six, that Myanmar is responsible for having committed a ",["genocide","https://doi.org/10.1080/10357718.2020.1813251"]," against the Rohingya in 2017, and had also failed to investigate and prosecute those responsible."]},{"k":"p","s":["In the landmark ruling, which came seven years after the case was filed, the court ordered Myanmar must provide restitution and compensation to the victims of its “clearance operations” in Rakhine State in 2017."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is the ",["first time","https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2026/11/historic-un-ruling-that-myanmar-committed-genocide-against-rohingya-is-rare-victory-for-survivors/"]," since the adoption of the ",["UN genocide convention","https://treaties.un.org/doc/publication/unts/volume%2078/volume-78-i-1021-english.pdf"]," in 1948 that the court has found a state responsible for committing genocide."]},{"k":"h","s":["Why the case matters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Twice before, however, the ICJ has ruled on the merits of a genocide claim."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2007, the court found Bosnian Serb forces had committed genocide at ",["Srebrenica","https://www.icj-cij.org/case/91"]," in 1995 during the Bosnian War, but that Serbia itself was not responsible for it. It concluded instead that Serbia had failed to prevent the genocide and punish those responsible."]},{"k":"p","s":["And in 2015, the ICJ ",["dismissed","https://www.icj-cij.org/case/118"]," Croatia’s claim and Serbia’s counter-claim over crimes committed during the conflict after the breakup of Yugoslavia in the 1990s. The court found serious crimes had occurred, but there was not the intent to destroy a group that genocide requires."]},{"k":"p","s":["The case against Myanmar was already significant because it set a new precedent for ",["who can bring cases","https://eastasiaforum.org/2026/03/17/the-icj-rohingya-case-reshapes-human-rights-litigation/"]," to the ICJ."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Gambia, a small African nation with no direct connection to the Rohingya, brought Myanmar before the court under the ",["genocide convention","https://www.ohchr.org/en/instruments-mechanisms/instruments/convention-prevention-and-punishment-crime-genocide"]," in 2019. Three years later, the judges ",["accepted","https://www.aspistrategist.org.au/international-court-rejects-myanmars-bid-to-halt-genocide-case/"]," that any party to the treaty can enforce it."]},{"k":"p","s":["This reasoning will be considered carefully in another ",["genocide case","https://www.icj-cij.org/pending-cases"]," currently before the court, brought by South Africa against ",["Israel","https://www.theguardian.com/law/2026/nov/19/myanmar-ruling-new-relevance-genocide-convention-messages-israel"]," over its actions in Gaza."]},{"k":"h","s":["How did we get here: attacking the Rohingya"]},{"k":"p","s":["Following attacks by a Rohingya armed group, Myanmar’s military launched a wave of what it called “ ",["clearance operations","https://doi.org/10.1080/10357718.2020.1813251"],"” in northern Rakhine State in late 2017. Many thousands of Rohingya civilians were killed, hundreds of women and girls were raped, villages were burned and more than 740,000 people fled to neighbouring Bangladesh."]},{"k":"p","s":["But genocide has a narrow legal meaning, and mass violence alone is not enough. The acts must be carried out with the intent to destroy the group, in whole or in part."]},{"k":"p","s":["While it is possible to gather evidence of the physical acts of genocide, proving intent is difficult. Genocidal plans are rarely recorded in official documents."]},{"k":"p","s":["The court had to infer Myanmar’s intentions from its conduct. The court made clear that an intention to destroy can coexist with other intentions. What matters is whether the inference of genocide explains all of the evidence taken together."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["Myanmar military","https://impunitywatch.com/merits-hearings-end-in-icj-genocide-case-between-the-gambia-and-myanmar/"]," and former Myanmar leader ",["Aung San Suu Kyi","https://eastasiaforum.org/2020/03/26/the-folly-of-aung-san-suu-kyis-bad-apple-defence/"]," did not deny that people died. Instead, they argued they were fighting terrorism and had no intent to destroy the Rohingya ethnic group."]},{"k":"p","s":["Myanmar also argued the case is “ ",["flawed and unfounded","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/1/14/myanmar-says-rohingya-genocide-case-at-the-hague-is-flawed-unfounded"],"”, ",["claiming","https://www.reuters.com/world/asia-pacific/myanmar-tells-world-court-gambia-has-not-proven-rohingya-genocide-case-2026-01-16/"]," it was committed to returning and resettling the Rohingya from Bangladesh."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ICJ rejected Myanmar’s arguments. It found much of what the military did could not be explained by fighting an insurgency."]},{"k":"p","s":["There was no evidence it distinguished between civilians and fighters, for example. Men and boys were executed, women and girls were raped on a mass scale, babies and small children were targeted, villages were burned methodically, and people were shot at as they fled their homes."]},{"k":"p","s":["The only reasonable inference to draw from the evidence, the court held, was an intention to destroy the Rohingya of northern Rakhine State."]},{"k":"h","s":["Restitution ordered for victims"]},{"k":"p","s":["The court therefore ordered Myanmar must investigate and, where warranted, prosecute those responsible for committing the genocide, including military commanders. It must prohibit genocide in its national law, and provide guarantees this will not happen again. It must also allow the return of displaced Rohingya and the reunification of families, and it must return or replace their property."]},{"k":"p","s":["Myanmar must also help search for the disappeared and rebury the dead, provide physical and psychological rehabilitation to victims, and protect the Rohingya from further discrimination and persecution. Where these acts of restitution cannot fully repair the damage, Myanmar must offer compensation to the Rohingya, both individually and collectively."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ICJ settles disputes between states and does not try individuals for their actions. However, prosecutors at the International Criminal Court have ",["sought an arrest warrant","https://news.un.org/en/story/2024/11/1157536"]," for ",["Min Aung Hlaing","https://time.com/article/2026/09/23/myanmar-president-interview-Min-Aung-Hlaing/"],", Myanmar’s former commander in chief, for alleged crimes against humanity."]},{"k":"p","s":["Its judges have ",["yet to rule","https://www.fortifyrights.org/reg-inv-2026-09-09/"]," on that request. The ICJ decision may open the door to future prosecutions of individuals for genocide and other crimes against humanity."]},{"k":"h","s":["Myanmar today"]},{"k":"p","s":["Min Aung Hlaing led the 2021 coup that overthrew Aung San Suu Kyi’s government and became president this April, after elections ",["widely dismissed","https://www.amnestyusa.org/press-releases/myanmar-presidency-must-not-shield-min-aung-hlaing-from-being-held-accountable/"]," as a sham."]},{"k":"p","s":["Five Southeast Asian governments have since ",["received him","https://www.manilatimes.net/2026/10/28/world/asia-oceania/the-philippines-top-diplomat-leads-a-humanitarian-mission-to-myanmar/2456301"],". The United States, which has ",["declared","https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/21/us-to-declare-myanmar-army-committed-genocide-against-rohingya"]," the atrocities against the Rohingya a genocide, has joined them. A senior US state department official ",["met with Min Aung Hlaing","https://www.channelnewsasia.com/asia/us-direct-talks-myanmar-generals-6441696"]," in Myanmar in September. In addition, a published ",["US strategy","https://www.internazionale.it/ultime-notizie-reuters/2026/11/02/us-strategy-links-myanmar-peace-talks-to-rare-earth-access"]," has linked peace talks to access to Myanmar’s rare earths."]},{"k":"p","s":["Despite the legal victory in the ICJ, the Rohingya remain in perilous conditions. Those still in Rakhine State continue to ",["experience torture, abuse and discrimination","https://news.un.org/en/story/2026/08/1168200"]," from the Myanmar military and the Arakan Army, an ethnic armed group which controls most of the state."]},{"k":"p","s":["And more than a million Rohingya remain in ",["worsening conditions","https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/19/world/asia/myanmar-genocide-refugee-camp.html"]," in camps in Bangladesh."]},{"k":"h","s":["What happens next?"]},{"k":"p","s":["The court has kept the case open to decide further on the amount of compensation to be paid. Myanmar has two years to report back to the court on the steps it has taken to comply with the judgement. The ruling by the ICJ is final and binding, but the court has no police force or security services to enforce it."]},{"k":"p","s":["The UN Security Council can take steps to compel Myanmar to abide by the decision under ",["Article 94","https://www.un.org/en/about-us/un-charter/chapter-14"]," of the UN Charter, though it has ",["never previously taken this step","https://www.un.org/en/ga/sixth/80/pdfs/statements/ilc/31mtg_icj_president.pdf"],". And Myanmar’s backers on the Security Council, China and ",["Russia","https://www.lowyinstitute.org/the-interpreter/myanmar-s-junta-finds-a-second-patron-in-moscow"],", have routinely provided the junta ",["with diplomatic cover","https://press.un.org/en/2007/sc8939.doc.htm"],". Whether this support will survive the court’s conclusion that Myanmar has committed genocide remains to be seen."]},{"k":"p","s":["China is keen to be seen as a responsible global citizen, so this decision may impact its level of diplomatic support for Myanmar’s military government, although geography and history will ensure it remains ",["engaged","https://eastasiaforum.org/2025/11/16/myanmars-military-regime-gains-ground-as-the-world-tilts-towards-authoritarianism/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Russia, having been brought in from the cold by the US under ",["US President Donald Trump","https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/nov/19/apec-summit-trump-xi-putin-meeting-shenzhen-china"],", will also be keen to avoid being seen to condone genocide. However, defence and security cooperation between the two countries is likely to continue."]},{"k":"p","s":["Southeast Asia is where diplomatic shifts are most likely. The ASEAN bloc of 11 Southeast Asian nations has recently indicated it could pursue “ ",["calibrated engagement","https://www.scmp.com/news/asia/southeast-asia/article/3374989/angry-over-indignity-myanmar-review-future-ties-asean"],"” with Myanmar, but the ICJ finding may make that more difficult. Any country pursing normalisation of ties with Myanmar will face significant pressure from the ",["European Union","https://www.eeas.europa.eu/eeas/myanmar-statement-spokesperson-judgement-international-court-justice_en"]," to disengage."]},{"k":"p","s":["The same government that was found to have attempted the destruction of the Rohingya people is now required to act as the guarantor of their safety."]},{"k":"p","s":["For now, the court has done what it can, as has The Gambia in bringing the case. Ensuring Myanmar takes up the task of implementing the court’s orders now rests with all states, including those that have so far preferred to look away."]}],"chars":7577},"https://theconversation.com/what-it-was-like-to-watch-crucial-cop-climate-talks-fall-apart-at-the-last-minute-297270":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-23T08:06Z","sha":"4db0590ebe0366168131d9110de8082c3b4727e4d6383670f151f8287a7a7495","read":"https://theconversation.com/what-it-was-like-to-watch-crucial-cop-climate-talks-fall-apart-at-the-last-minute-297270","bytes":180189,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"What it was like to watch crucial COP climate talks fall apart at the last minute","by":[{"n":"Miki Perkins","r":"Environment & Energy Editor"}],"pub":"2026-11-23T06:05:02Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["It was a day-and-a-half past the official deadline when the UN climate summit COP31 began to unravel in earnest."]},{"k":"p","s":["On Sunday morning, the corridors inside the huge expo-style venue in the Turkish city of Antalya were almost empty. Tired groups of delegates and media sat propped against the walls waiting for updates, charging their phones and drinking coffee. Many had barely slept. Australian Energy Minister Chris Bowen – who headed up the COP31 negotiations – reportedly slept for ",["only a few minutes","https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/nov/23/cop31-left-chris-bowen-stuck-between-petrostates-and-climate-reality-but-the-failure-to-say-the-f-word-is-not-his-alone"]," on the final night, as delegates kept waking him."]},{"k":"p","s":["The talks dragged well into overtime to become the longest summit on record. But it would not finish the way co-presidents Bowen and Turkish Environment Minister Murat Kurum had hoped."]},{"k":"p","s":["A third draft of the proposed agreement had been released overnight. But it still made no mention of the crucial words “fossil fuels”, “oil,” “coal,” or “phase out.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["Suddenly, a media huddle formed and German Climate Minister Carsten Schneider appeared, looking grim. Before the final plenary had even begun, he confirmed Germany would reject the agreement, telling reporters it was a “step backward”."]},{"k":"p","s":["Shortly afterwards, the European Union followed suit, in a dramatic intervention during the plenary from Ireland’s Climate Minister Darragh O'Brien. The text had failed to meet the moment he told the assembled countries: “We will not endorse a decision […] that does not even mention fossil fuels.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["Journalists were shuttling between the meeting and talking to delegates in the halls, trying to establish the extent of the dissent. A BBC reporter somehow continued a live cross as he ran down the hallway after delegates from the EU and Iceland."]},{"k":"p","s":["Inside the meeting, Panama announced it was out. This was not surprising – the country’s environment minister had said the world was “held hostage by ",["fossil fuels","https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/nov/18/world-held-hostage-by-oil-mafia-says-panama-minister-at-cop-31"],"”, ruefully declaring “we are in love with our kidnappers.” The Marshall Islands soon followed, and the United Kingdom too. The number of countries grew."]},{"k":"p","s":["By now, it was clear: the COP31 negotiations to reach an agreement had collapsed."]},{"k":"h","s":["What now?"]},{"k":"p","s":["This year’s conference was my first in person, though I’d covered a number from a distance. For two weeks, I’d listened to discussions and press conferences, interviewed Bowen and commissioned academic experts to explain the ",["labyrinthine world of these UN summits","https://theconversation.com/yes-the-cop-climate-talks-are-far-from-perfect-but-they-still-hold-the-power-for-change-295350"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["In an interview with ",["Bowen","https://theconversation.com/a-clear-call-for-climate-action-bowen-defends-albanese-at-cop31-296545"],", he sang the praises of Australia and Turkey’s signature ",["“35 by 35” electrification pledge","https://theconversation.com/the-world-needs-to-get-serious-about-electrification-heres-why-296062"],". Electric vehicles, heat pumps and batteries are more efficient than fossil fuel precursors, and cut emissions. But the pace of change is too slow, he said. Bowen was less keen to talk fossil fuels, after Prime Minister Anthony Albanese ",["failed to mention","https://theconversation.com/a-clear-call-for-climate-action-bowen-defends-albanese-at-cop31-296545"]," the words in his opening remarks."]},{"k":"p","s":["While Bowen and his Turkish counterparts could not ",["get the","https://theconversation.com/the-cop31-climate-summit-is-betting-on-electrification-but-still-needs-a-plan-to-ditch-fossil-fuels-295493"]," electrification goal embedded in the agreement, more than than 75 countries and 180 businesses signed on outside the official process, including the EU and China."]},{"k":"p","s":["In the last three days, the COP process became a rollercoaster. Nobody knew when the next agreement draft might drop. Minister and negotiators delayed their flights once, then twice. Bowen’s office went quiet as he holed up in negotiations. The clearest sign talks would stretch over another night was the daily email from organisers about late-night catering options. I joined other media at the site all weekend, waiting for news."]},{"k":"p","s":["The UN climate talks are no stranger to division. There are longstanding arguments between developed and developing countries, petrostates and those pushing for rapid action away from fossil fuels."]},{"k":"p","s":["Agreements have to be made by consensus, meaning a tiny minority of opposing states can stop progress. But consensus has been reached before, most notably producing the 2015 Paris Agreement to hold climate change well below 2°C. In 2023, the world’s governments even managed to mention the “F” word – fossil fuels – in the ",["final text","https://unfccc.int/news/cop28-agreement-signals-beginning-of-the-end-of-the-fossil-fuel-era"]," for the first time in decades of trying to stop climate change."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even as climate change ",["accelerates","https://doi.org/10.1029/2025GL118804"]," and a giant El Niño ",["threatens crops","https://fews.net/global/special-report/october-2026"]," ",["around the world","https://joint-research-centre.ec.europa.eu/jrc-news-and-updates/el-nino-drives-crop-failure-central-america-and-east-africa-and-threatens-next-season-southern-2026-09-03_en"],", the divisions were too great. And the fallout has begun. Civil society leaders are describing it as one of the most ",["dismal COP failures yet","https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/nov/22/cop31-failed-transition-away-from-fossil-fuels-inevitable"],". The Coalition in Australia is calling on Bowen ",["to resign","https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/nov/23/anthony-albanese-digital-duty-of-care-labor-greens-coalition-one-nation-angus-taylor-pauline-hanson-penny-wong-ai-ntwnfb?page=with%3Ablock-6b0370ae8f08268116cd578d#block-6b0370ae8f08268116cd578d"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["As recriminations begin, more and more people will ask whether these talks are worth it. What’s the point of flying thousands of people around the world to meet when consensus on something as fundamental as fossil fuels cannot be reached?"]},{"k":"p","s":["I’ve covered environment and climate for years. It’s not a round known for uplifting news, but every day I’m immensely grateful to work on such urgent stories. And surprisingly, today I’m not feeling too glum."]},{"k":"p","s":["Globally, change is underway. China’s ",["emissions","https://www.economist.com/leaders/2026/11/12/chinas-emissions-are-falling-thank-self-interest"]," are now falling due to intense domestic effort to boost solar, wind, electric vehicles and batteries. Pakistan is installing solar as ",["fast as possible","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.erss.2026.105016"]," to bypass its expensive, failing grid, while ",["Ethiopia","https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2025/sep/12/ethiopia-electric-vehicle-power-petrol-diesel-cars-dam-green-energy"]," and ",["Nepal","https://www.climatechangenews.com/2026/04/02/nepals-ev-revolution-pays-off-as-oil-crisis-causes-pain-at-the-pumps/"]," are pushing hard on EVs to avoid paying for oil. The Iran war cut supply of petrol, diesel and other fossil fuel products, driving up prices."]},{"k":"p","s":["The failed COP31 draft agreement had some good points, such as recognising climate science and underlining the importance of oceans. But if we’d witnessed the world sign up to a cowardly cover text in Antalya that didn’t even mention fossil fuels it would have felt like real failure. This COP’s inability to land a cover decision has laid bare the consequences of failing to hold the fossil fuel industry accountable. And that feels like a breath of fresh air."]},{"k":"p","s":["Multilateralism was still on show in the final days as over 130 countries – from the EU to Pacific Island nations to the least developed countries – pushed back against an unsatisfactory draft."]},{"k":"p","s":["During the summit, I witnessed passionate people from all over the world come together with hope and ingenuity in a truly global meeting, and that was humbling. These meetings are the only forum where developing countries, those bearing the full brunt of the climate crisis, can look rich countries in the eye and demand change."]},{"k":"p","s":["These UN summits are not the only forum for climate action. Dozens of nations focused on phasing out fossil fuels met for the first time ",["this year","https://transitionawayconference.com/reports"],". Next year, Tuvalu and Ireland will host the second conference with a growing coalition of countries, a complement to UN climate negotiations."]},{"k":"p","s":["Let’s end on the words of Tuvalu’s climate minister, Maina Talia: “We will not allow inaction and obstruction to dampen our resolve. We will advance where we can with those willing to show up.”"]}],"chars":6602}};
